%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 7c7c947f0ccabb24dbf991df8e9f6d4f, type: 3}
  m_Name: org & mode of inservice
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  defaultQuestions:
  - QuestionText: Which national-level organization is the apex body for designing
      models for in-service teacher education in India?
    Options:
    - UGC
    - NCERT
    - CBSE
    - NCTE
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: org & mode of inservice
  - QuestionText: 'The primary agency responsible for in-service training of elementary
      teachers at the district level is the:'
    Options:
    - SCERT
    - NUEPA
    - NIOS
    - DIET
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: org & mode of inservice
  - QuestionText: Which of the following is a face-to-face mode of in-service teacher
      education?
    Options:
    - Participating in a SWAYAM MOOC
    - Attending a national seminar on educational technology
    - Reading a professional journal
    - Contributing to an online forum
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: org & mode of inservice
  - QuestionText: 'The organization that conducts refresher courses for university
      and college teachers through Academic Staff Colleges is the:'
    Options:
    - NCERT
    - AICTE
    - NCTE
    - UGC
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: org & mode of inservice
  - QuestionText: What is the primary function of a Block Resource Centre (BRC)?
    Options:
    - To regulate university education
    - To provide grassroots-level support and training to teachers in a block
    - To develop national curriculum frameworks
    - To award Ph.D. degrees in education
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: org & mode of inservice
  - QuestionText: A group of teachers meeting every week to analyze student work
      and plan lessons is an example of which mode?
    Options:
    - Distance Education
    - A Professional Learning Community (PLC)
    - An Induction Program
    - A Refresher Course
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: org & mode of inservice
  - QuestionText: 'The state-level nodal agency for in-service teacher education
      is the:'
    Options:
    - DIET
    - CRC
    - NCERT
    - SCERT
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: org & mode of inservice
  - QuestionText: Which mode of in-service education is characterized by its flexibility
      and use of digital platforms like SWAYAM?
    Options:
    - Workshop mode
    - Distance and Online mode
    - Seminar mode
    - Conference mode
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: org & mode of inservice
  - QuestionText: 'The organization that focuses on training educational administrators
      and planners is:'
    Options:
    - NCERT
    - NIEPA
    - NCTE
    - DIET
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: org & mode of inservice
  - QuestionText: 'A teacher systematically investigating why students are struggling
      with fractions in her own classroom is engaged in:'
    Options:
    - A workshop
    - Peer coaching
    - A seminar
    - Action research
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: org & mode of inservice
  - QuestionText: 'The most decentralized unit for organizing in-service teacher
      education is the:'
    Options:
    - National level
    - State level
    - School level
    - District level
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: org & mode of inservice
  - QuestionText: Which of the following is a key feature of the workshop mode?
    Options:
    - It is primarily a one-way lecture.
    - It is highly interactive and focuses on hands-on skill development.
    - It is always conducted online.
    - It has no specific objectives.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: org & mode of inservice
  - QuestionText: 'The CRC (Cluster Resource Centre) coordinator typically acts as
      a:'
    Options:
    - National policy maker
    - Mentor and resource person for teachers in a cluster of schools
    - University professor
    - School principal
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: org & mode of inservice
  - QuestionText: Which mode is best for introducing a large number of teachers to
      a new national curriculum framework like NEP 2020?
    Options:
    - Self-study
    - Lesson study
    - Peer mentoring
    - Large-scale orientation programs
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: org & mode of inservice
  - QuestionText: 'The organization of in-service teacher education in India is best
      described as a:'
    Options:
    - Centralized system with no state involvement
    - Decentralized, multi-level structure
    - System managed solely by private agencies
    - Non-existent structure
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: org & mode of inservice
  - QuestionText: 'A program designed specifically for teachers who are newly appointed
      is called a(n):'
    Options:
    - Refresher course
    - Seminar
    - Workshop
    - Induction program
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: org & mode of inservice
  - QuestionText: Which online platform, launched by the Government of India, provides
      free MOOCs for teacher professional development?
    Options:
    - NPTEL
    - SWAYAM
    - e-PG Pathshala
    - DIKSHA
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: org & mode of inservice
  - QuestionText: 'The primary advantage of school-based in-service education is
      its:'
    Options:
    - High cost
    - Immediate relevance to the specific school context
    - Isolation from other schools
    - Focus on theoretical knowledge only
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: org & mode of inservice
  - QuestionText: Which of the following is a collaborative mode of in-service education?
    Options:
    - Reading a book alone
    - Watching a pre-recorded webinar
    - Participating in a lesson study with colleagues
    - Taking an online test
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: org & mode of inservice
  - QuestionText: 'The role of NCERT in the organization of in-service education
      is primarily:'
    Options:
    - Administrative control over state programs
    - Development of resource materials and training of master trainers
    - Direct training of every school teacher
    - Funding all state-level programs
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: org & mode of inservice
  - QuestionText: 'A ''refresher course'' is primarily aimed at:'
    Options:
    - Newly recruited teachers
    - Updating and renewing the knowledge of experienced teachers
    - Parents and community members
    - School dropouts
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: org & mode of inservice
  - QuestionText: Which mode is most suitable for a teacher who lives in a remote
      area with limited internet access?
    Options:
    - Online webinars
    - MOOCs
    - Correspondence courses through NIOS
    - Professional Learning Communities (PLCs)
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: org & mode of inservice
  - QuestionText: The DIETs are mandated to focus on the training of teachers at
      which level?
    Options:
    - Secondary and Senior Secondary only
    - Elementary level (Classes I-VIII)
    - Higher Education only
    - Pre-primary only
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: org & mode of inservice
  - QuestionText: 'Observing a colleague''s class and providing constructive feedback
      is a key component of:'
    Options:
    - Distance learning
    - Peer coaching
    - A national conference
    - Self-directed learning
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: org & mode of inservice
  - QuestionText: 'The organization of in-service training through BRCs and CRCs
      ensures:'
    Options:
    - That training is removed from the local context
    - A complete separation of pre-service and in-service education
    - That only national-level experts are involved
    - Greater reach and accessibility for teachers at the grassroots
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: org & mode of inservice
  - QuestionText: Which of the following is a self-directed mode of professional
      development?
    Options:
    - Attending a mandatory workshop
    - Voluntarily reading research articles on a new teaching strategy
    - Participating in a state-organized orientation
    - Being part of a mandated PLC
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: org & mode of inservice
  - QuestionText: 'The main purpose of an ''orientation program'' is to:'
    Options:
    - Provide a long vacation for teachers
    - Familiarize teachers with new policies, curricula, or textbooks
    - Replace pre-service teacher education
    - Evaluate teachers for promotion
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: org & mode of inservice
  - QuestionText: Which national mission aims to strengthen in-service teacher training
      through an integrated online platform?
    Options:
    - SSA (Sarva Shiksha Abhiyan)
    - RMSA (Rashtriya Madhyamik Shiksha Abhiyan)
    - NISHTHA (National Initiative for School Heads' and Teachers' Holistic Advancement)
    - RTE (Right to Education)
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: org & mode of inservice
  - QuestionText: 'A key challenge in the organization of in-service education in
      India is:'
    Options:
    - Lack of any structural framework
    - Inadequate coordination between national, state, and district levels
    - Over-reliance on school-based modes
    - Absence of online platforms
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: org & mode of inservice
  - QuestionText: 'The mode of in-service education that involves a cycle of collaborative
      planning, teaching, observing, and revising a lesson is known as:'
    Options:
    - Action Research
    - Workshop
    - Peer Coaching
    - Lesson Study
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: org & mode of inservice
  - QuestionText: Which body is responsible for recognizing and regulating teacher
      education programs, which indirectly influences in-service education?
    Options:
    - NCERT
    - NCTE
    - UGC
    - AIU
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: org & mode of inservice
  - QuestionText: Which mode is most effective for the rapid dissemination of a new
      teaching technique to a large number of teachers across the country?
    Options:
    - One-on-one mentoring
    - Action research projects
    - School-based PLCs
    - Large-scale workshops and online MOOCs
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: org & mode of inservice
  - QuestionText: 'The success of school-based in-service education largely depends
      on the leadership of the:'
    Options:
    - District Education Officer
    - School Principal
    - SCERT Director
    - NCERT Chairman
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: org & mode of inservice
  - QuestionText: 'A ''seminar'' as a mode of in-service education typically involves:'
    Options:
    - Only listening to a single expert
    - Presentation of papers and discussion on a specific theme
    - Hands-on practice of skills
    - Isolated individual work
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: org & mode of inservice
  - QuestionText: 'The primary goal of the multi-level organization of in-service
      education is to:'
    Options:
    - Create bureaucratic hurdles
    - Ensure a top-down, uniform approach
    - Cascade training effectively from national to grassroots level
    - Eliminate the need for teacher input
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: org & mode of inservice
  - QuestionText: Which of the following is an advantage of online modes like webinars?
    Options:
    - They require no internet connectivity.
    - They allow for participation from geographically dispersed locations.
    - They are always more effective than face-to-face interaction.
    - They eliminate the need for any preparation.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: org & mode of inservice
  - QuestionText: 'The "cascade model" of training, often used in Indian in-service
      education, refers to:'
    Options:
    - Training a master cadre of resource persons who then train others
    - A waterfall of information with no feedback
    - Training only one teacher per school
    - A model used exclusively for pre-service education
    CorrectOptionIndex: 0
    LevelName: org & mode of inservice
  - QuestionText: A teacher attending a course to learn a new language would be participating
      in which type of in-service education?
    Options:
    - Content upgradation
    - Pedagogical training
    - Orientation program
    - Induction program
    CorrectOptionIndex: 0
    LevelName: org & mode of inservice
  - QuestionText: 'The organization of in-service education at the cluster level
      (through CRCs) helps in promoting:'
    Options:
    - Isolation among teachers
    - Peer learning and sharing of local best practices
    - Dependence on national experts only
    - Standardized teaching without variation
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: org & mode of inservice
  - QuestionText: Which mode is characterized by its focus on solving a specific,
      localized classroom problem through a systematic process?
    Options:
    - Conference
    - Distance Education
    - Refresher Course
    - Action Research
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: org & mode of inservice
  - QuestionText: The DIKSHA portal is an initiative for teacher training that primarily
      uses which mode?
    Options:
    - Only face-to-face workshops
    - A digital platform for hosting training modules and resources
    - International student exchange
    - Print-based correspondence
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: org & mode of inservice
  - QuestionText: 'A limitation of the ''cascade model'' of organization is that:'
    Options:
    - It is too cheap and efficient
    - It does not have a national-level component
    - It involves teachers directly from the start
    - The quality of training may dilute as it moves down the levels
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: org & mode of inservice
  - QuestionText: Which of the following is a formal mode of in-service education?
    Options:
    - Informal discussion in the staff room
    - A UGC-sponsored refresher course at an Academic Staff College
    - Independently watching a YouTube tutorial
    - Reading a newspaper article on education
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: org & mode of inservice
  - QuestionText: 'The most significant role of a teacher in a self-directed mode
      is that of a(n):'
    Options:
    - Passive recipient
    - Autonomous and proactive learner
    - Implementer of directives
    - Bystander
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: org & mode of inservice
  - QuestionText: 'The organization of in-service education aims to create a:'
    Options:
    - Culture of dependency on experts
    - System with no accountability
    - Static teaching workforce
    - Culture of continuous professional learning
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: org & mode of inservice
  - QuestionText: 'A ''conference'' as a mode is particularly useful for:'
    Options:
    - In-depth skill practice
    - Networking and exposure to a wide range of ideas and innovations
    - One-on-one mentoring
    - Isolated reflection
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: org & mode of inservice
  - QuestionText: 'The effectiveness of any mode of in-service education ultimately
      depends on:'
    Options:
    - The number of certificates awarded
    - The fame of the resource person
    - The cost of the program
    - Its impact on improving teacher practice and student learning
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: org & mode of inservice
  - QuestionText: 'A blend of face-to-face and online modes is known as:'
    Options:
    - Single-mode delivery
    - Blended learning
    - Distance learning
    - Isolated learning
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: org & mode of inservice
  - QuestionText: 'The primary focus of organizational efforts at the SCERT level
      is to:'
    Options:
    - Ignore national frameworks
    - Manage individual school finances
    - Work only on pre-service education
    - Adapt and contextualize national programs for the state
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: org & mode of inservice
